  ],
  "text": "Noise cancelling works by playing the exact opposite of the noise, in real time. It is not blocking anything. No extra padding is doing the work. A microphone on the outside hears the noise arriving. The electronics flip it upside down. Every peak becomes a trough. Then it plays that back into your ear, and the two add up to almost nothing. Which only works if it can predict what comes next, and it has microseconds to do it. A steady engine drone is completely predictable. It repeats, low and forever. So it disappears. That is the part that feels like magic on a plane. A voice does not repeat, it is high frequency, and it changes constantly. Which is why the engine vanishes and the person two rows back does not. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
